# Demo capture "race" (tools/video/capture.sh race): the same start as demo-boot, then the menu route
# of gp-50cc.cmds (fresh profile -> new licence -> Single Player -> Grand Prix -> 50cc -> Mario,
# Standard Kart M, automatic -> Mushroom Cup -> Luigi Circuit) and a race driven with the keyboard
# and mouse: left click held is accelerate, A/D steer. The driver is a script, not a player: it
# follows a fixed timeline, so a few bumps are expected after the first corner. Marks: page, start, title, main-menu,
# race-ok (the OK that loads the race), go (the countdown's GO, when accelerate is pressed).
mark page
waitstart 90000
mark start
wait 2500
eval document.getElementById('hide-controls').click()
wait 17000
# opening -> title -> Select License -> new licence -> Choose a Mii -> confirm -> ready -> guest note
click 500 430
wait 400
mark title
wait 2500
click 500 430
wait 3000
click 500 430
wait 2500
click 500 430
wait 3000
click 500 430
wait 2500
click 500 430
wait 4000
click 500 430
wait 4000
click 500 430
wait 4000
mark main-menu
# Single Player -> Grand Prix -> 50cc -> Mario -> kart -> automatic drift -> Mushroom Cup -> OK
click 500 430
wait 3000
click 500 430
wait 3000
click 500 430
wait 4000
click 500 430
wait 3500
click 500 430
wait 3500
click 500 430
wait 3500
click 500 430
wait 3000
mark race-ok
click 500 430
# Course flyover, then the countdown; "3" came 15.5 to 18 s after the OK on two captures, so the
# flyover's length varies by about two seconds. Holding A from "3" burns the kart out, so
# accelerate is pressed at +20.3 s: the "1" or the GO, whichever it is this time. `go` marks the
# press and the video cuts in a few seconds before it.
wait 20300
mark go
mousedown 500 430
# The first corner is a left-hander about 8 s after the start: steer through it, then straight on.
wait 8300
keydown a
wait 2400
keyup a
wait 136000
mouseup
mark end
wait 500
